  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The new case `examples/catalog/2d/contour-tabs` obeys `examples/catalog/README.md`. It has `model/` with the generator script and the mesh, `build.camscript`, `contour-tabs.camproj`, `contour-tabs.nc` and `README.md`.\n- The part is a 90 x 50 x 6 mm plate with four 10 mm corner chamfers. The generator script writes it. The geometry is original (Clean-Room Protocol).\n- One 2D Contour cuts the plate out of a 120 x 80 x 6 mm sheet with `EM-0600-4FL`. The lead-in is a 3 mm arc. The lead-out is a 4 mm line. There are four tabs, 8 mm wide and 2 mm high.\n- `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs` has one new test and one helper for it. No product code changes.\n- `docs/decisions/2859-contour-tabs-example.md` records the choices.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had only the seed case `2d/first-part`. No case showed a 2D Contour with lead moves and tabs (#2392).\n\n## Readings of the posted program\n\n- The levels are `Z4`, `Z2` (the tab top) and `Z0`.\n- `Z4` and `Z2` each cut the whole ring: one `G03` lead-in, one `G01` lead-out, one lift.\n- `Z0` is four runs. Each run has one `G03` lead-in and one `G01` lead-out. The tool lifts over each tab (three lifts to `Z11`, the last to `Z21`).\n- No block goes below `Z0`.\n- `cam.verify()` in the script reports no problem.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `contour_tabs_case_posts_the_lead_moves_and_the_tab_lifts` (`camcraft-app`, binary `example_catalog`). It counts the lead-in arcs for each level, the lifts, the linear block before each lift, and the four tab lifts at `Z0`.\n- Red before the change: yes. Without the case folder the test fails (`case 2d/contour-tabs must hold .../contour-tabs.nc`).\n- Mutation: case folder removed: red. Case folder restored: green. There is no new guard in product code, so there is no other mutation.\n- The two tests that were there before read the new case too: `every_catalog_case_opens_regenerates_verifies_and_posts_byte_for_byte` and `every_catalog_case_rebuilds_from_camscript`. They pass.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: `checked 2d/contour-tabs`, `checked 2d/first-part`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green on the head `e240dad1d` (1 step, `app suites: example_catalog`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` shows only the new file `contour-tabs.nc`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The program did not run on a machine or in a control simulator.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --screenshots` and `--pdf` did not run.\n- No heavy lane ran. The diff changes no product code.\n- Windows and macOS did not run.\n\n## Found during the work\n\n- #2876: `add_operation` refuses `lead: { arc: ... }` because the merge patch keeps the seeded linear lead. The message does not name the cause. The script uses `lead: { linear: null, arc: { radius: 3.0 } }`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `examples/catalog/` or `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`.\n\nChangelog: Examples: the catalog case `2d/contour-tabs` shows a 2D Contour with an arc lead-in, a linear lead-out and four tabs.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2859\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
